---
/**
 * The meter's colours, read the way a cockpit's are: green normal, amber caution, red warning. The
 * swatches are the XDJ-RX2's own LED colours, so they show a signal state like every lit colour
 * on the site.
 */
---

<section class="code" aria-labelledby="colour-code">
  <h2 id="colour-code">The meter’s colours</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><span class="swatch" data-zone="green"></span><span><strong>Green:</strong> normal, with room to spare.</span></li>
    <li>
      <span class="swatch" data-zone="orange"></span><span
        ><strong>Orange:</strong> caution. The loudest parts of a track belong on the first two orange lights.</span
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="swatch" data-zone="red"></span><span
        ><strong>Red:</strong> warning. The sound may distort, and the recording keeps it.</span
      >
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<style>
  .code {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    background: var(--paper-2);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.75rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .swatch {
    width: 1.5rem;
    height: 0.75rem;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
    transform: translateY(0.05rem);
  }

  .swatch[data-zone='green'] {
    background: var(--led-g);
  }

  .swatch[data-zone='orange'] {
    background: var(--led-a);
  }

  .swatch[data-zone='red'] {
    background: var(--led-r);
  }

  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .swatch {
      forced-color-adjust: none;
    }
  }
</style>
